{
  "_help": [
    "MAP DATA FILE. Edit numbers here to move things; no code changes needed. The game reloads when you save.",
    "Units are metres. x runs from stairwell A (x=0 is the stairwell A fire door, at the library end) toward stairwell B (the exit end).",
    "z is across the building: negative z = LEFT side when walking A to B, positive z = RIGHT side. The hallway centre line is z=0.",
    "Measurements come from the evacuation plans and clips in references/walkthrough (see LABELS.md there). Floor 1 has no plan, so it is estimated.",
    "floor: 0 (basement), 1, 2 or 3. Half floors (0.5, 1.5, 2.5) are the stair half-landings. Both stairwells run from floor 0 to floor 3.",
    "BASEMENT (floor 0, ids start b0_): feet at y = -3.6, ceilings settings.basementCeilingHeight. It has no light fixtures and no breaker panel; it stays dark all game.",
    "ROOMS: x,z is the corner with the smallest x and z; w is the size along x; d is the size along z. Or give 'shape' as a list of [x,z] corners.",
    "  floorMat: concrete | carpet.  ceiling: smooth | tile | vault | none.  lights: drum | panel | lantern | none.",
    "  Walls are built automatically around every room. Rooms that share an edge share one wall.",
    "DOORS: x,z is the centre of the door, and it must sit exactly on a room edge. wallAlong says which way that wall runs ('x' or 'z').",
    "  type: wood | woodWindow | fire | woodGlass | glassBlack | exit | elevator | opening (no door, just a gap) | glassPanel (fixed glass) | barrier.",
    "  locked: true makes it a locked door. message is what the player reads when trying it. connects lists the two rooms it joins.",
    "settings.exitDoor is the id of the exit door. It opens only once every breaker panel has power. Change it to make another door the exit.",
    "PANELS: one breaker panel per floor. x,z is the point on the wall face where the panel's back sits; rot is the way its front faces (same as facingDeg); y (optional) is the height of its centre above the floor (default 1.4).",
    "  The number of fuses placed in the building equals the number of panels.",
    "keySpawns: the places where fuses can appear. At the start, one distinct random entry is picked per fuse. y is the height above the floor.",
    "settings.objective: holdTime = seconds E is held to reset a breaker; noiseRadius = metres the reset is heard (it always reaches the monster, any floor);",
    "  alertDelay = seconds until a despawned monster returns after a reset; sightBonus = extra metres the monster sees on a powered floor;",
    "  respawnCutPerPanel = seconds removed from its respawn gap per powered panel; respawnMinGap = the gap never goes below this.",
    "facingDeg: 0 = looking toward B, 90 = looking toward the right side, 180 = toward A, 270 = toward the left side.",
    "In the game: the top-left readout shows the room id and your x / z, and M shows the map, so you can report or fix positions.",
    "HIDING SPOTS: camY is the eye height while hidden; door (optional) is a door id that closes behind the player. PROPS: furniture, see src/world/props.js for the types."
  ],

